IMPORT prelude

-- Land Revenue Collection Act 1940 (Singapore) -- when unpaid land revenue (premium, rent, royalty, charges and fees on land owed to
-- the State) becomes an arrear, and the Collector's sale of the land by auction to recover it: notice and its timing, the upset
-- price, stopping the sale by paying, the purchaser's deposit and balance, when the sale becomes final, resale on default,
-- reversion to the State when no bid is enough, the surplus, annulment by the Commissioner of Lands or the court with 6% interest,
-- the time bars, the measure of the defaulter's damages, and the defaulter's pleas (ss 2, 4 to 8, 10 to 14, 16, 17, 19 to 24, 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/LRCA1940.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is "Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022" against s 22(1).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0152 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Act is short, so nearly all of its operative Parts 1 to 3 are taken. Not encoded: the Collector's appointment (s 2(2)), place
-- of sale (s 9), costs recoverable as arrears (s 15, beyond the upset price), personal service mechanics (s 25), the rule-making
-- and fees provisions (ss 27, 27A), the State's right to sue (s 28), and the Schedule forms. Calendar months are taken as a number
-- supplied by the caller; calendar arithmetic is not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the writing-l4-rules skill as shown in
-- earlier naive rows (the skill itself was not loadable in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Revenue Collection Act 1940 -- auction for arrears`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 and 4 -- land revenue, arrears and defaulters`

-- s 2(1): "land revenue" means "every sum now due or which hereafter becomes due to the State on account of premium, rent, royalty,
-- charges and fees of any kind chargeable in respect of land"; "proprietor" includes a lessee of State land.
-- s 4(1): "every annual rent ... shall be due and payable on 1 January in any year, and any such rent if not sooner paid shall become
-- an arrear on 1 April in the year in respect of which it is due, and any other form of land revenue shall become an arrear on the
-- 15th day after service of notice" in the First Schedule form. (4): "Every person liable to pay an arrear shall be a defaulter."
DECLARE Charge IS ONE OF
    `annual rent`
    `premium`
    `royalty`
    `survey fees`
    `income tax`
    `a parking fine`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the charge is land revenue` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `income tax` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a parking fine` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The month of the year (1 to 12) in which the question is asked; rent for that year is in arrear from 1 April.
GIVEN `month of the year` IS A NUMBER, `rent paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual rent is an arrear` IF
    (NOT `rent paid`) AND `month of the year` AT LEAST 4

-- Days counted from the day of service of the First Schedule notice; the arrear arises "on the 15th day after service".
GIVEN `days since service of the demand` IS A NUMBER, `other revenue paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `other land revenue is an arrear` IF
    (NOT `other revenue paid`) AND `days since service of the demand` AT LEAST 15

-- s 4(2): rent for the year of alienation "shall be calculated proportionately from the date of alienation to the end of the year
-- and is payable on or before the date of alienation". Whether the day of alienation counts is not said; the caller supplies the
-- day count (an inference that it is a simple day-pro-rating).
GIVEN `annual rent` IS A NUMBER, `days from alienation to year end` IS A NUMBER, `days in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rent for the year of alienation` MEANS
    `annual rent` TIMES `days from alienation to year end` DIVIDED BY `days in the year`

§§ `5 and 6 -- notice of sale and public notice`

-- s 5(2)(a): "it shall not be necessary to serve a notice of sale on any proprietor of any land who is not resident in the district
-- in which the land is situate". (3): "no failure to serve or irregularity in serving any notice of sale ... shall invalidate any
-- sale" or give a cause of action against the Government; it is only to be considered by the Commissioner under s 19.
GIVEN `proprietor resides in the district` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice of sale must be served on the proprietor` IF
    `proprietor resides in the district`

GIVEN `notice of sale was served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failure to serve the notice invalidates the sale` IF
    FALSE

-- s 6(1): the auction date is "not less than 3 calendar months after the date of the first posting of the notice"; (2): the notice
-- "shall be published in the Gazette on a date not less than 4 weeks prior to the date of the sale" (4 weeks taken as 28 days).
GIVEN `months from first posting to sale` IS A NUMBER, `days from Gazette to sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale date meets the notice periods` IF
    `months from first posting to sale` AT LEAST 3 AND `days from Gazette to sale` AT LEAST 28

§§ `7, 8, 10 -- upset price, stopping the sale, deposit`

-- s 7(1): the land is put to auction "at an upset price sufficient to cover the arrear due in respect thereof together with fees
-- due and costs and shall be sold to the highest bidder".
GIVEN `arrear` IS A NUMBER, `fees` IS A NUMBER, `costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the upset price` MEANS `arrear` PLUS `fees` PLUS `costs`

-- s 8: "If any person tenders to the Collector at any time previous to a sale the amount of the arrear ... together with fees due
-- and costs, the Collector shall upon receipt thereof desist from the sale". Any person, not only the defaulter.
GIVEN `tendered before the sale` IS A NUMBER, `arrear` IS A NUMBER, `fees` IS A NUMBER, `costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector must stop the sale` IF
    `tendered before the sale` AT LEAST `the upset price` `arrear` `fees` `costs`

-- s 10: the purchaser must "deposit in cash immediately 25% on the amount of his bid, and in default of such deposit the land shall
-- forthwith be put up again for sale".
GIVEN `bid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash deposit` MEANS `bid` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `bid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balance of the purchase money` MEANS `bid` MINUS `the cash deposit` `bid`

§§ `11, 12, 13 -- balance, finality, default`

-- s 11: the balance is paid "on or before the expiry of 3 months after the date on which the sale ... took place".
-- s 12: the sale "shall become final and conclusive on the expiry of 3 months from the date thereof unless" (a) the balance is
-- unpaid; (b) a court has annulled it by order served on the Collector by then; (c) the Commissioner of Lands has annulled it under
-- s 19; or (d) a court order extending the period or staying finality has been served on the Collector.
GIVEN `months since the sale` IS A NUMBER, `balance paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `annulled by the court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `annulled by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `court order extending the period served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is final and conclusive` IF
        `months since the sale` AT LEAST 3
    AND `balance paid`
    AND (NOT `annulled by the court`)
    AND (NOT `annulled by the Commissioner`)
    AND (NOT `court order extending the period served`)

-- s 13(1): "In default of payment of the balance within the prescribed period, the deposit shall be forfeited to the State, the land
-- shall be resold and the defaulting purchaser shall forfeit all claim to the land or to any part of the sum ... for which it may
-- subsequently be sold."
GIVEN `months since the sale` IS A NUMBER, `balance paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposit is forfeited and the land resold` IF
    `months since the sale` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `balance paid`)

§§ `14 -- title, registration and fraudulent dealing`

-- s 14(1): once final, the purchaser takes "free from all encumbrances created over it and from all subordinate interests derived
-- from it, except such as are expressly reserved by the Collector at the time of the auction". (4): registration of the conveyance
-- "shall be free of any fee or stamp duty". (5): knowingly and with fraudulent intent dealing with a cancelled lease, grant,
-- encumbrance, right or interest is deemed the offence in s 415 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating), or an attempt.
GIVEN `sale is final` IS A BOOLEAN, `interest reserved by the Collector at the auction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser takes free of the interest` IF
    `sale is final` AND (NOT `interest reserved by the Collector at the auction`)

GIVEN `dealt with a cancelled interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN, `with fraudulent intent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is deemed cheating under Penal Code s 415` IF
    `dealt with a cancelled interest` AND `knowingly` AND `with fraudulent intent`

§§ `16, 17 -- reversion to the State, surplus`

-- s 16(1): "if at any sale ... there is no bid sufficient to cover the amount due for the arrear together with fees and costs due",
-- once recorded in the Rent Auction Sale Book, "the land shall revert to and vest in the State and all right, title and interest of
-- the defaulter ... shall cease". The defaulter receives nothing: the Act provides no payment on reversion.
GIVEN `highest bid` IS A NUMBER, `arrear` IS A NUMBER, `fees` IS A NUMBER, `costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land reverts to the State` IF
    `highest bid` LESS THAN `the upset price` `arrear` `fees` `costs`

-- s 17: proceeds go first to "the arrear together with fees and costs due", and any surplus is paid to a claimant whose right
-- satisfies the Collector, or else held in trust; the proviso lets the Collector apply it to arrears on "any other land belonging
-- to the same owner within Singapore".
GIVEN `proceeds` IS A NUMBER, `arrear` IS A NUMBER, `fees` IS A NUMBER, `costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surplus` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 (`proceeds` MINUS `the upset price` `arrear` `fees` `costs`)

§§ `19, 22(2) -- annulment and the 6% refund`

-- s 19(1): the Commissioner of Lands may, "at any time before a sale ... has become final and conclusive upon proof to his
-- satisfaction that the sale was had contrary to the provisions of this Part and that material irregularities occurred or that any
-- proprietor or other person will suffer excessive hardship by reason of the sale, annul the sale"; proviso: no order "after the
-- date of institution of proceedings in court for the annulment of the sale".
-- READING (a fork): the grounds are taken as (contrary to the Part AND material irregularities) OR excessive hardship. The other
-- reading, contrary to the Part AND (irregularities OR hardship), would refuse annulment for hardship after a regular sale.
GIVEN `sale is final` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary to Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN, `material irregularities` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `excessive hardship` IS A BOOLEAN, `court proceedings instituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may annul the sale` IF
        (NOT `sale is final`)
    AND (NOT `court proceedings instituted`)
    AND (    (`contrary to Part 2` AND `material irregularities`)
         OR  `excessive hardship`)

-- s 19(2) and s 22(2): on annulment by the Commissioner or the court, "the purchase money or deposit paid by the purchaser shall be
-- refunded by the Government with interest at the rate of 6% per annum and the purchaser shall have no further claim". Simple
-- interest by days over 365 is an inference; the Act does not say how the interest runs.
GIVEN `amount paid` IS A NUMBER, `days held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund to the purchaser` MEANS
    `amount paid` PLUS `amount paid` TIMES 6 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `days held` DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `20, 21, 24 -- court challenges and time bars`

-- s 20: "any person interested" disputing the validity of a sale "may within 3 months of the date of the sale apply to the General
-- Division of the High Court to annul the sale". s 21(1): notwithstanding the Limitation Act 1959, no such suit after that period
-- "except in the case of fraud to which the purchaser is proved to be a party"; proviso: the title of a bona fide owner, mortgagee
-- or lessee for value from the purchaser is unaffected. s 24: only in the General Division of the High Court.
DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `a District Court`
    `a Magistrate's Court`

GIVEN `forum` IS A Forum, `months after the sale` IS A NUMBER, `purchaser party to fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `land now held by a bona fide taker for value from the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a suit to annul the sale can be maintained` IF
        `forum` EQUALS `the General Division of the High Court`
    AND (NOT `land now held by a bona fide taker for value from the purchaser`)
    AND (`months after the sale` AT MOST 3 OR `purchaser party to fraud`)

-- s 21(2): no suit for damages against the State or an officer "after the expiry of 3 months after the date of the sale except in
-- the case of actual fraud to which any officer of the State employed in or about the sale is proved to be a party or unless it is
-- proved that the sum ... was not in fact an arrear at the date of the sale".
GIVEN `forum` IS A Forum, `months after the sale` IS A NUMBER, `officer party to actual fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sum was not in fact an arrear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a damages suit is in time` IF
        `forum` EQUALS `the General Division of the High Court`
    AND (`months after the sale` AT MOST 3 OR `officer party to actual fraud` OR `sum was not in fact an arrear`)

§§ `22(1) -- substantial injury and the measure of damages`

-- s 22(1): no annulment or damages "except only upon the grounds of its having been made contrary to the provisions of this Act and
-- then only upon proof that the claimant has sustained substantial injury by reason of the irregularity", and the defaulter recovers
-- "as special damages for the irregularity the difference between the price actually obtained and the price which, in the opinion
-- of the court, would have been obtained at the Collector's sale if there had been no irregularity and no more".
GIVEN `contrary to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `substantial injury proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the irregularity can found relief` IF
    `contrary to the Act` AND `substantial injury proved`

-- Where the court's price is lower than the price obtained there is no loss; nil is an inference from "difference" and "no more".
GIVEN `price obtained` IS A NUMBER, `price the court finds without irregularity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the defaulter's special damages` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 (`price the court finds without irregularity` MINUS `price obtained`)

§§ `23 -- the defaulter's pleas`

-- s 23: no claim to rebate, remission or deferment of rent "unless the same has been allowed by the written authority of the
-- Commissioner of Lands", and no private demand against the Government, bars a sale; nor does the plea that the defaulter's money
-- sufficient to pay was in the Collector's hands "unless that money stands in the defaulter's name alone and without dispute and
-- unless after application in due time made by the defaulter the Collector has neglected or refused on insufficient grounds to
-- transfer it".
GIVEN `rebate allowed in writing by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rebate claim can bar the sale` IF
    `rebate allowed in writing by the Commissioner`

GIVEN `money held covers the arrear` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the defaulter's name alone` IS A BOOLEAN, `undisputed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `defaulter applied in due time` IS A BOOLEAN, `Collector refused on insufficient grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the money-in-hand plea can bar the sale` IF
        `money held covers the arrear`
    AND `in the defaulter's name alone`
    AND `undisputed`
    AND `defaulter applied in due time`
    AND `Collector refused on insufficient grounds`

§§ `26 -- substituted service`

-- s 26(1): where the Collector is satisfied the noticee "is keeping out of the way for the purpose of avoiding service" or the notice
-- cannot be served personally under s 25(3), he may in writing order service by affixing on the land and in a public place, or
-- otherwise; (3): such service "shall be as effectual as if it had been made on the noticee personally".
GIVEN `noticee avoiding service` IS A BOOLEAN, `personal service failed` IS A BOOLEAN, `written order of the Collector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `substituted service is as effectual as personal service` IF
    (`noticee avoiding service` OR `personal service failed`) AND `written order of the Collector`
